<div class="page">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:40rem;">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="overline">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">Refund Policy</h1>
      <p class="section-sub">Last updated <%= getYear() %></p>
    </div>

    <div class="stack" style="gap:var(--sp-6);">
      <div class="alert alert-success">
        Lifetime access carries a 7-day money-back guarantee. If it is not working for you, tell us
        within seven days of payment and we will refund it.
      </div>

      <section>
        <h2 class="card-title">How to request one</h2>
        <ol class="muted" style="margin-top:var(--sp-2);display:grid;gap:var(--sp-2);padding-left:1.2rem;">
          <li>Email <a href="mailto:support@upscbooks.shop">support@upscbooks.shop</a> from the address on your account.</li>
          <li>Tell us what went wrong — a bug, a device that won't work, or simply a change of plan.</li>
          <li>We process approved refunds to the original payment method within 5–7 working days.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="card-title">After a refund</h2>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-top:var(--sp-2);">
          Your lifetime access is switched off and your reading progress is retained, so if you return
          later you can pick up where you left off.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="card-title">Duplicate charges</h2>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-top:var(--sp-2);">
          The service refuses to take a second payment from an account that already has access, so a
          duplicate charge is a fault on our side. Contact us and it will be reversed in full.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="card-title">Not covered</h2>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-top:var(--sp-2);">
          We cannot refund a request made more than seven days after the payment date. We also cannot
          refund for a title you finished reading — but the seven days exist precisely so you can find
          that out before you commit.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <div class="row" style="margin-top:var(--sp-10);">
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>